<h2 id="user-content-faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<div class="faq-list">
    <details class="acc" open>
        <summary>Why was Dotkernel refactored to use the new PHP 5.5 Password Hashing API? <span class="chev">+</span></summary>
        <div class="acc-body">
            <p class="mb-0">To use the new Password Hashing functions introduced in PHP 5.5 and unify all password related functions used for both admin and users, Dotkernel's codebase was refactored in version 1.8.0, starting from revision 799.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
    <details class="acc">
        <summary>How can PHP versions older than 5.5 use these new hashing functions? <span class="chev">+</span></summary>
        <div class="acc-body">
            <p class="mb-0">Since the 4 new functions are only available since PHP 5.5, Dotkernel used the Password Compatibility library (ircmaxell/password_compat).</p>
        </div>
    </details>
    <details class="acc">
        <summary>What is the minimum PHP version required after this change? <span class="chev">+</span></summary>
        <div class="acc-body">
            <p class="mb-0">The minimum PHP version required to run Dotkernel was raised to PHP 5.3.8.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
    <details class="acc">
        <summary>What steps are needed to apply this refactor to an older Dotkernel system? <span class="chev">+</span></summary>
        <div class="acc-body">
            <p class="mb-0">Change the password column definition in the admin and user tables via ALTER TABLE, remove the settings.admin.salt entry from application.ini, apply the provided patch, and run the conversion script described in Console/Controller.php at line 47.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
    <details class="acc">
        <summary>What happens to existing admin passwords during the upgrade? <span class="chev">+</span></summary>
        <div class="acc-body">
            <p class="mb-0">Admin passwords cannot be converted automatically, so they need to be recreated manually.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
